 "deviations": "Two deliberate deviations from the plan's literal section-3.1 sketch, both toward higher fidelity to the REAL feed contract (inspected in feed/src/retrieval/types.ts and feed/scripts/feedq.ts, not guessed):\n\n1. FeedRetrieveHit.features is typed as the full FeedRetrieveFeatures shape (bm25, tier, tier_mult, aggregator, aggregator_mult, quality, quality_mult, age_days, recency_mult, chunker_ver) rather than the plan's simplified `Record<string, number>` \u2014 the real feed RetrieveFeatures has non-numeric fields (tier is a 1|2|3 union, aggregator is boolean, quality is a string enum, chunker_ver is a string), so the plan's shorthand would have been a lossy mirror of the actual contract this ticket is supposed to mirror.\n\n2. `retrieve(query, opts?)` \u2014 opts made optional (plan sketch shows it as required) since a mandate-blind unfiltered query needs no flags at all; this matches how the real feedq CLI itself treats all retrieve flags as optional.\n\nOne important observation, not a deviation but worth flagging to the coordinator: feed/scripts/feedq.ts's actual CLI has only ONE error exit path today (exit 1, plain stderr text, no JSON error envelope) \u2014 there is no exit-2 usage-error distinction the way dossierq's bin has. The client still implements the full 0/1/2 exit-code mapping specified in the plan (parity with dossierq-client, and free to keep in case feedq ever adds a usage-error path), but as of this campaign's feedq, the FeedqUsageError branch is only reachable via the injected-runner fixture test, never a real subprocess call. Also: FeedqQueryError carries only a message (no `code` field like DossierqQueryError) because feedq's exit-1 path never emits a JSON error object to parse a code from, only raw stderr text.\n\nThe trace?: FeedTraceRecorder parameter is implemented exactly as instructed: accepted in FeedqClientOptions, held in closure scope, documented as a C2 placeholder, and never invoked anywhere in this module (no trace file, no record()/flush() call). Its interface is defined locally in feedq-retrieve-client.ts (not in types.ts, since types.ts is scoped to the Feed response mirror per the ticket) and is expected to be superseded when C2 lands the real trace.ts.\n\nNo other files were touched. git status in the worktree shows only new files (pipeline/src/services/feed/, pipeline/test/feedq-retrieve-client.test.ts) plus an append to the pre-existing untracked implementation-notes-feed-slice2b.md; nothing else in the tree was modified. No git commands were run (add/commit/push), per instructions."
